---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '~/lib/site';

/**
 * Supplied as finished copy — the text below is verbatim. Only the wrapper was
 * adapted to this repo: BaseLayout instead of Layout, container-prose +
 * prose-alltech instead of the .legal classes, and the postal address and phone
 * number now come from site.ts so they cannot drift from the rest of the site.
 *
 * RESOLVED: Section 15 originally listed legal@askalltech.com, which does not
 * route anywhere — notices sent to it, including the permission requests
 * Sections 2 and 5 tell people to send, would have landed nowhere. Confirmed
 * with the team and repointed at the monitored shared mailbox,
 * hello@askalltech.com (the same address assessment submissions deliver to).
 * Note help@askalltech.com is deliberately NOT used here: it is reserved for
 * existing customers.
 */

const effectiveDate = 'July 29, 2026';
const addr = site.address;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms governing use of askalltech.com, the AllTech security gap assessment, and related online tools."
  canonical={`${site.url}/terms`}
>
  <section class="surface-dark py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="container-prose">
      <header class="mb-10">
        <div class="eyebrow mb-4">Legal</div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight" style="color: var(--color-text-primary);">
          Terms of Use
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-sm" style="color: var(--color-text-subtle);">
          Effective date: {effectiveDate}
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-alltech legal-body">
        <p>
          These Terms of Use (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) govern your access to and use of
          <a href={site.url}>askalltech.com</a> and any related pages, forms, assessments, and
          online tools we make available (together, the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;), operated by AllTech
          (&ldquo;AllTech,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;). By using
          the Site, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Site.
        </p>

        <h2 id="not-agreement">1. The Site is not a services agreement</h2>
        <p>
          The Site describes services we offer. It does not create a client relationship, a quote,
          or a binding commitment to provide services. Managed IT, cybersecurity, network, cloud,
          and installation services are governed exclusively by a signed Master Services Agreement,
          statement of work, quote, or similar written agreement between AllTech and the client. If
          anything on the Site conflicts with a signed agreement, the signed agreement controls for
          that client.
        </p>

        <h2 id="eligibility">2. Eligibility and acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least 18 years old and able to form a binding contract. You agree not to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Access or attempt to access any portion of the Site, our systems, or our clients&rsquo;
            systems without authorization, including by scanning, probing, or testing for
            vulnerabilities.
          </li>
          <li>
            Introduce malware, launch denial-of-service attacks, or otherwise interfere with the
            Site&rsquo;s operation or security controls.
          </li>
          <li>
            Scrape, harvest, or systematically extract content or contact details, including for
            training machine learning models, without our written permission.
          </li>
          <li>
            Submit false, misleading, or third-party information through our forms, or use them to
            transmit spam or unsolicited solicitations.
          </li>
          <li>
            Reverse engineer, decompile, or circumvent any technical measure protecting the Site.
          </li>
          <li>Use the Site in violation of any applicable law or regulation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Authorized security testing of AllTech systems requires our prior written consent and a
          defined scope. Contact us before conducting any testing.
        </p>

        <h2 id="assessment">3. Security gap assessment</h2>
        <p>
          Our free security gap assessment is a high-level, self-reported questionnaire. It is
          provided for general informational purposes only.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            The score reflects only the answers you supply. We do not verify them, and we do not
            scan, test, or inspect your environment as part of the assessment.
          </li>
          <li>
            The assessment is not a penetration test, vulnerability assessment, audit, or
            certification, and it is not evidence of compliance with CIS, NIST, HIPAA, PCI DSS,
            CMMC, cyber-insurance requirements, or any other framework or standard.
          </li>
          <li>
            A high score does not mean you are secure, and a low score does not mean you have been
            compromised. Do not rely on the assessment as the sole basis for any security,
            insurance, procurement, or compliance decision.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="content">4. Informational content</h2>
        <p>
          Content on the Site — including service pages, case studies, blog and insights posts, and
          framework references — is general information, not professional, legal, regulatory, or
          insurance advice for your specific environment. Case studies describe past engagements and
          do not guarantee comparable results. Availability, response times, service levels, and
          pricing are set in a signed agreement, not on the Site.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ip">5. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Site and its content — text, graphics, logos, layouts, code, methodologies, and the
          &ldquo;AllTech Top 10&rdquo; and related materials — are owned by AllTech or its licensors
          and are protected by intellectual property laws. You may view and print pages for your own
          internal business evaluation. Any other reproduction, distribution, modification,
          republication, or commercial use requires our prior written permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Third-party names and marks appearing on the Site, including Cloudflare, Ubiquiti UniFi,
          Microsoft, Microsoft 365, Entra ID, and Datto, are the property of their respective
          owners. Their appearance indicates the technologies we work with and does not imply
          endorsement by those owners except where a partner relationship is expressly stated.
        </p>
        <p>
          Client logos appear with permission and remain the property of those organizations.
        </p>

        <h2 id="submissions">6. Your submissions</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for anything you send us through the Site. Do not submit confidential
          information belonging to a third party, credentials, or sensitive personal information
          through the contact or assessment forms. Information you submit is handled in accordance
          with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you send us feedback or suggestions,
          you grant us a perpetual, royalty-free license to use them without obligation or
          attribution.
        </p>

        <h2 id="third-party">7. Third-party sites and tools</h2>
        <p>
          The Site links to properties we do not control, including our remote assistance
          portal and embedded maps. We are not responsible for their content, availability,
          or practices, and links do not imply endorsement. Access to remote assistance and
          other support tools is limited to authorized client personnel and is subject to
          the applicable services agreement and any tooling vendor&rsquo;s terms.
        </p>

        <h2 id="availability">8. Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Site at any time without notice. We
          do not warrant that the Site will be uninterrupted, timely, secure, or error-free, or that
          content is current or accurate.
        </p>

        <h2 id="warranty">9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p>
          THE SITE AND ALL CONTENT, ASSESSMENTS, AND TOOLS ARE PROVIDED &ldquo;AS IS&rdquo; AND
          &ldquo;AS AVAILABLE,&rdquo; WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. TO THE
          FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, ALLTECH DISCLAIMS ALL IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING
          MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, AND ANY
          WARRANTY ARISING FROM COURSE OF DEALING OR USAGE OF TRADE. THIS SECTION DOES NOT LIMIT ANY
          WARRANTY EXPRESSLY GIVEN IN A SIGNED SERVICES AGREEMENT.
        </p>

        <h2 id="liability">10. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, ALLTECH AND ITS OWNERS, OFFICERS, EMPLOYEES, AND
          SUPPLIERS WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL,
          EXEMPLARY, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, REVENUE, DATA, GOODWILL, OR
          BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO YOUR USE OF THE SITE, EVEN IF ADVISED
          OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
        </p>
        <p>
          OUR TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THE SITE WILL NOT EXCEED ONE
          HUNDRED U.S. DOLLARS ($100). LIABILITY ARISING FROM SERVICES IS GOVERNED SOLELY BY THE
          APPLICABLE SIGNED SERVICES AGREEMENT. SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW CERTAIN EXCLUSIONS,
          SO SOME OF THE ABOVE MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU.
        </p>

        <h2 id="indemnity">11. Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify and hold harmless AllTech and its owners, officers, and employees
          from any claims, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable
          attorneys&rsquo; fees) arising out of your use of the Site, your violation of these Terms,
          or your violation of any law or third-party right.
        </p>

        <h2 id="law">12. Governing law and venue</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Utah, without regard to its
          conflict-of-laws rules. You consent to the exclusive jurisdiction and venue of the state
          and federal courts located in Cache County, Utah for any dispute arising out of or
          relating to the Site or these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2 id="general">13. General</h2>
        <p>
          If any provision of these Terms is held unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in
          effect. Our failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver of it. These Terms, together
          with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, are the entire agreement between you and
          AllTech regarding the Site. You may not assign these Terms; we may assign them in
          connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets. Sections 5, 6, and 9 through 13
          survive termination.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">14. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms at any time. Changes take effect when posted, and we will update
          the effective date above. Your continued use of the Site after a change constitutes
          acceptance.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">15. Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>AllTech</strong><br />
          {addr.street}<br />
          {addr.city}, {addr.region} {addr.postalCode}<br />
          Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phoneE164}`}>{site.phone}</a><br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:hello@askalltech.com">hello@askalltech.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Numbered sections are deep-linked from within the page and from elsewhere,
     so headings need to clear the sticky header when jumped to. */
  .legal-body :global(h2),
  .legal-body :global(h3) {
    scroll-margin-top: 6rem;
  }
</style>
